[
  {
    "question": "Why are responses so slow when running small local models like Qwen 3.5 4B/9B with Ollama in Hermes?",
    "answer": "Hermes sends the full tool schema (~45 tools) on every API call, resulting in a large number of input tokens that small 4B–9B models struggle to process quickly. To improve performance, you can disable unused toolsets with `hermes tools`, use a faster quantization, switch to a larger model (32B+), or set `terminal.backend: local` in configuration to reduce container overhead."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Hermes Agent support automatic smart model routing to send simple queries to cheaper models?",
    "answer": "No. Under maintainer policy, Hermes does not support complexity-based automatic model routing, cheap-versus-strong model tiers, or per-turn provider/model overrides. The primary session model and provider are retained. Subagent models can still be configured via `delegation.provider` and `delegation.model` in `config.yaml`, and models can be switched manually using `/model` or CLI flags."
  },
  {
    "question": "Why does my Telegram bot return an HTTP 401 error when configured with a local Ollama endpoint?",
    "answer": "When `provider` is set to `auto`, Hermes scans environment variables for existing API keys (such as `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`) and routes requests to the external provider instead of your local Ollama instance. To resolve this, explicitly set `provider: custom` alongside your `base_url` in `~/.hermes/config.yaml` to disable automatic provider detection."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is there a web interface available to use Hermes Agent directly in a browser?",
    "answer": "Yes. Hermes includes a first-party web dashboard that embeds the full TUI in a browser Chat tab. You can launch it by running `hermes dashboard`, which starts a local web server at `http://127.0.0.1:9119` and opens it in your browser."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can the Hermes Discord bot process uploaded text and Python code files?",
    "answer": "Yes. Authorized Discord file uploads are cached by Hermes, and text-readable files—including `.txt` and `.py` scripts—are automatically injected into the agent's prompt."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should security vulnerabilities in Hermes Agent be reported?",
    "answer": "Vulnerabilities should not be submitted as public GitHub issues. Instead, report them privately via GitHub Security Advisories or by emailing security@nousresearch.com with the submission details outlined in Section 1 of `SECURITY.md`."
  },
  {
    "question": "What happens when Hermes hits its tool-call limit, and how can long autonomous tasks continue?",
    "answer": "When `agent.max_turns` (default 90) is reached, Hermes requests a final response without further tool executions rather than silently failing. You can increase the turn limit using `hermes chat --max-turns <N>` or updating `agent.max_turns` in config. For long multi-turn autonomous work, use the persistent `/goal` command, which persists across sessions and can be resumed with `/goal resume`."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is native Windows supported without WSL2?",
    "answer": "Yes. Windows 10/11 is a Tier 1 supported platform installed via the official PowerShell installer (`install.ps1`) without requiring WSL. However, WSL2 is still recommended if you need the embedded POSIX PTY terminal pane in the web dashboard's `/chat` interface."
  },
  {
    "question": "How do I configure Hermes Agent to connect to Azure AI Foundry?",
    "answer": "Azure AI Foundry can be configured via `hermes setup`, which auto-detects the `ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_BASE_URL` environment variable, or by setting `provider: azure-foundry` directly in your configuration. Claude Code-specific variables like `CLAUDE_CODE_USE_FOUNDRY` and `ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL` are not used by Hermes."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I submit a pull request to add a new memory backend to the core `plugins/memory/` directory?",
    "answer": "No. In-tree additions to `plugins/memory/` are closed per `CONTRIBUTING.md`. New memory providers must be published as standalone plugins installed to `~/.hermes/plugins/` or via pip entry points implementing the `MemoryProvider` abstract base class (`sync_turn`, `prefetch`, `shutdown`, and optional `post_setup`). Once published, you can submit a documentation PR to list it in the Community plugins section."
  },
  {
    "question": "How does Hermes Agent handle multi-agent task execution and per-channel personas?",
    "answer": "Multi-agent coordination is handled via the `delegate_task` tool, which spawns isolated child `AIAgent` instances with their own contexts and toolsets (supporting up to 3 concurrent subagents by default). Per-channel personas are configured using the `channel_prompts` configuration key, which sets distinct system prompts per channel ID across Discord, Telegram, Slack, and Mattermost."
  },
  {
    "question": "How can I view tool call chains, parameters, and outputs like in Langsmith?",
    "answer": "Hermes provides a bundled, opt-in Langfuse observability integration. You can enable it by running `hermes plugins enable observability/langfuse` or via `hermes tools`, which generates turn-level traces, nested observations, and logs tool inputs and outputs."
  },
  {
    "question": "How do I resolve `[Errno 13] Permission denied` errors when running Hermes in Docker on a NAS (such as UGOS Pro, Synology, or unRAID)?",
    "answer": "You can pass `PUID` and `PGID` (or `HERMES_UID` and `HERMES_GID`) environment variables (for example, `PUID=1000` and `PGID=10`) to the Docker container. Hermes uses these variables at startup to remap its internal runtime user and group permissions to match your host NAS bind-mount storage."
  },
  {
    "question": "Why am I being charged API token costs for Claude instead of using my Claude Pro/Max subscription?",
    "answer": "Anthropic bills all third-party API key usage as API billing regardless of whether you have an active Pro or Max subscription. To utilize your Pro or Max subscription allowance with Hermes Agent, authenticate using OAuth rather than entering an API key."
  },
  {
    "question": "Why does Telegram reject messages with an 'Unauthorized user' warning even when `allowed_chats` is configured?",
    "answer": "`allowed_chats` only specifies allowed group chat IDs, not user authorization. To authorize direct messages from a specific user, configure `allow_from` with the user ID under `telegram:` in `~/.hermes/config.yaml` (which sets `TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS`), use the pairing flow by running `hermes pairing approve telegram <CODE>`, or set `allow_all: true` to allow all users."
  }
]
